  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653 acc. The RNA modality is clearly dominant (0.48–0.65) while image-only is very weak (0.21 with resnet50). The key untested question is whether the image modality, despite its low standalone accuracy, provides complementary signal when fused with the strong RNA representation. config_032 is the most direct extension of the current best: it keeps scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer (the proven RNA pipeline) and adds resnet50 image features via concat fusion. This isolates the fusion benefit with the simplest fusion strategy. If it beats 0.653, the remaining 3 experiments can explore weighted fusion or ViT image encoder to push further. If it does not, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and can use remaining budget to fine-tune the RNA pipeline. This is the highest-value exploration step given 3 experiments remain."
}

